The other altar camping method is the prayer cycle.  Its
goal is both protection and books.  The good news is for
XP=3DN it tries N times to give you a spell you don't know
yet in a school you do know.  Being XP=3D30 there's not a
bad chance that almost all of the spellbooks for a while
will be new ones in your own schools.  It gives a high
chance you'll get create familiar.  Doing that form of
altar camping is limited to food availability for any
character without hungerless casting.

Thing is you have one wish left - "blessed spellbook of
creat familiar" is worth considering then read it when
you think its time to go for the ascension.  You'll want to
read it before your last dive and then read it again on the
way up to have the spell on the planes.  Spamming pets
who you can displace to progress is nicer than whacking
hostiles who get replaced much of the time before you
have a chance to step forward.

